"gloss":"Hodaviah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H5570","lemma":"סְנָאָה","tr":"se·na·ah","gloss":"Senaah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H3967","lemma":"מֵאָה","tr":"me·ah","gloss":"hundred","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":581}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NEH","chapter":7,"verse":73,"verseEnd":73,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"So the priests, Levites, gatekeepers, singers, and temple servants, along with some of the people and the rest of the Israelites, settled in their own towns. And by the seventh month the Israelites had settled in their towns.","from":2},{"book":"1CH","chapter":5,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"But they were unfaithful to the God of their fathers, and they prostituted themselves with the gods of the peoples of the land, whom God had destroyed before them.","from":1},{"book":"1CH","chapter":5,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"So the God of Israel stirred up the spirit of Pul king of Assyria (that is, Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria) to take the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh into exile. And he brought them to Halah, Habor, Hara, and the river of Gozan, where they remain to this day.","from":1},{"book":"NEH","chapter":7,"verse":64,"verseEnd":64,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"These men searched for their family records, but they could not find them and so were excluded from the priesthood as unclean.","from":1},{"book":"EZR","chapter":2,"verse":43,"verseEnd":43,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The temple servants: the descendants of Ziha, the descendants of Hasupha, the descendants of Tabbaoth,","from":2},{"book":"EZR","chapter":2,"verse":58,"verseEnd":58,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The temple servants and descendants of the servants of Solomon numbered 392 in all.","from":2},{"book":"EZR","chapter":2,"verse":70,"verseEnd":70,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So the priests, the Levites, the singers, the gatekeepers, and the temple servants, along with some of the people, settled in their own towns; and the rest of the Israelites settled in their towns.","from":2},{"book":"EZR","chapter":8,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"They also brought 220 of the temple servants, all designated by name. David and the officials had appointed them to assist the Levites.","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":5},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2}]},"10-13":{"people":[{"id":"jachin-h3199i","name":"Jachin","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"jedaiah-h3048g","name":"Jedaiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"joiarib-h3114g","name":"Joiarib","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"azariah-h5838l","name":"Azariah","kind":"person","brief":"High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"hilkiah-h2518h","name":"Hilkiah","kind":"person","brief":"A High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"meraioth-h4812g","name":"Meraioth","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"shallum-h7967l","name":"Shallum","kind":"person","brief":"High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"zadok-h6659i","name":"Zadok","kind":"person","brief":"High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"zerahiah-h2228g","name":"Zerahiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"adaiah-h5718i","name":"Adaiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"adiel-h5717h","name":"Adiel","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"immer-h0564g","name":"Immer","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"jahzerah-h3170","name":"Jahzerah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Meshullam","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"jeroham-h3395j","name":"Jeroham","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"maasai-h4640","name":"Maasai","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"malchijah-h4441h","name":"Malchijah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"meshillemith-h4921","name":"Meshillemith","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"meshullam-h4918m","name":"Meshullam","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"pashhur-h6583g","name":"Pashhur","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":12}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H4918","lemma":"מְשֻׁלָּם","tr":"me·shul·lam","gloss":"Meshullam","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":25},{"base":"H3080","lemma":"יְהוֹיָרִיב","tr":"ye·ho·ya·riv","gloss":"Jehoiarib","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H5717","lemma":"עֲדִיאֵל","tr":"a·di·el","gloss":"Adiel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H4812","lemma":"מְרָיוֹת","tr":"me·ra·vot","gloss":"Meraioth","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H3199","lemma":"יָכִין","tr":"ya·khin","gloss":"Jachin","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H5718","lemma":"עֲדָיָ֫הוּ","tr":"a·da·yah","gloss":"Adaiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H0564","lemma":"אִמֵּר","tr":"im·mer","gloss":"Immer","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H3395","lemma":"יְרֹחָם","tr":"ye·ro·cham","gloss":"Jeroham","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H3048","lemma":"יְדַעְיָה","tr":"ye·da·yah","gloss":"Jedaiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"H6583","lemma":"פַּשְׁחוּר","tr":"pash·chur","gloss":"Pashhur","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NUM","chapter":4,"verse":15,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Aaron and his sons have finished covering the holy objects and all their equipment, as soon as the camp is ready to move, the Kohathites shall come and do the carrying. But they must not touch the holy objects, or they will die. These are the transportation duties of the Kohathites regarding the Tent of Meeting. Eleazar son of Aaron the priest shall oversee the oil for the light, the fragrant incense, the daily grain offering, and the anointing oil. He has oversight of the entire tabernacle and everything in it, including the holy objects and their utensils.”","from":11},{"book":"NUM","chapter":4,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"This is the service of the Gershonite clans at the Tent of Meeting, and their duties shall be under the direction of Ithamar son of Aaron the priest.","from":11},{"book":"NUM","chapter":4,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"This is the service of the Merarite clans according to all their work at the Tent of Meeting, under the direction of Ithamar son of Aaron the priest.”","from":11},{"book":"2KI","chapter":23,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then the king commanded Hilkiah the high priest, the priests second in rank, and the doorkeepers to remove from the temple of the LORD all the articles made for Baal, Asherah, and all the host of heaven. And he burned them outside Jerusalem in the fields of Kidron and carried their ashes to Bethel.","from":11},{"book":"2KI","chapter":25,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The captain of the guard also took away Seraiah the chief priest, Zephaniah the priest of second rank, and the three doorkeepers.","from":11},{"book":"1CH","chapter":6,"verse":8,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Ahitub was the father of Zadok, Zadok was the father of Ahimaaz, Ahimaaz was the father of Azariah, Azariah was the father of Johanan, Johanan was the father of Azariah, who served as priest in the temple that Solomon built in Jerusalem, Azariah was the father of Amariah, Amariah was the father of Ahitub, Ahitub was the father of Zadok, Zadok was the father of Shallum,","from":11},{"book":"1CH","chapter":24,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Thus they were divided by lot, for there were officers of the sanctuary and officers of God among both Eleazarʼs and Ithamarʼs descendants.","from":11},{"book":"1CH","chapter":24,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the fifteenth to Bilgah, the sixteenth to Immer,","from":12}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"14-18":{"people":[{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"azrikam-h5840i","name":"Azrikam","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"hashabiah-h2811h","name":"Hashabiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"hasshub-h2815g","name":"Hasshub","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"merari-h4847","name":"Merari","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Levi","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"shemaiah-h8098e","name":"Shemaiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"asaph-h0623i","name":"Asaph","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"bakbakkar-h1230","name":"Bakbakkar","kind":"person","brief":"From Levi","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"galal-h1559g","name":"Galal","kind":"person","brief":"From Levi","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"heresh-h2792","name":"Heresh","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"mattaniah-h4983g","name":"Mattaniah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned musician","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"mica-h4316g","name":"Mica","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"zichri-h2147k","name":"Zichri","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"asa-h0609h","name":"Asa","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Elkanah","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"berechiah-h1296i","name":"Berechiah","kind":"person","br